---
import { changeClasses } from "../../data/how-i-work";
---
<div class="how-change-classes" aria-label="Change classes">
  {changeClasses.map((item) => (
    <article class={`how-change-class is-${item.key}`}>
      <header>
        <span>{item.label}</span>
        <small>{item.posture}</small>
      </header>
      <p>{item.examples}</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>planning</dt><dd>{item.planning}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>proof</dt><dd>{item.proof}</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>
  ))}
</div>
<p class="how-callout"><strong>When I am uncertain, I use the higher class.</strong> A short diff is not automatically low risk; permissions, credentials, networking, data, deployment, deletion and cost-bearing resources change the review posture.</p>
